# Notices for the Hyper Tuned adapters

## Training data

The adapters were trained in part on text derived from two public research
corpora of recorded meetings. The transcripts were processed (cut into turns,
cleaned and paired with target text) to make training examples. No audio and
no transcript is included in the adapter files.

- **AMI Meeting Corpus**, by the AMI project. Released under the Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Source:
  https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/. Changes were made.
- **ICSI Meeting Corpus** (transcripts), by the International Computer Science
  Institute. Released under CC BY 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Source:
  https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/icsi/. Changes were made.

The makers of the two corpora do not endorse Uhstray, Zerds or these adapters.

## Base models

The adapters contain no base model weights. Each one is loaded onto a base
model distributed by its own authors under the Apache License 2.0:

- Qwen3 0.6B and Qwen3 1.7B, by Alibaba Cloud (Qwen team).
- MiniCPM5-2B, by OpenBMB.

## Tools

The adapter files were converted to GGUF with llama.cpp (MIT License).
